	"chichenItzaTitle": "Hey there! I’m Lalit Sahu, and I’m glad you’re here.",
	"chichenItzaSubTitle": "Welcome",
	"chichenItzaRegionTitle": "I'm from Indore",
	"chichenItzaArtifactCulture": "Maya",
	"chichenItzaArtifactGeolocation": "North and Central America",
	"chichenItzaPullQuote1Top": "The Beauty Between",
	"chichenItzaPullQuote1Bottom": "the Heavens and the Underworld",
	"chichenItzaPullQuote2": "The Maya and Toltec vision of the world and the universe is revealed in their stone monuments and artistic works.",
	"chichenItzaPullQuote2Author": "UNESCO",
	"chichenItzaCallout1": "The site exhibits a multitude of architectural styles, reminiscent of styles seen in central Mexico and of the Puuc and Chenes styles of the Northern Maya lowlands.",
	"chichenItzaCallout2": "The Notary App, Application Developer, Bengaluru, India (Jul. 2024 - Oct. 2024)",
	"chichenItzaVideoCaption": "“Ancient Maya 101 | National Geographic.” Youtube, uploaded by National Geographic.",
	"chichenItzaMapCaption": "Map showing location of Chichen Itza in Yucatán State, Mexico.",
	"chichenItzaHistoryInfo1": "Hello! I’m Lalit Sahu, a passionate and driven software developer specializing in cross-platform application development and cybersecurity. Currently pursuing an Integrated MTech at Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal, I maintain a strong academic record with a CGPA of 8.68, and I am deeply committed to expanding my expertise in cutting-edge technologies. \nWith hands-on experience as an Application Developer at TheNotaryApp, I excel in creating user-centric applications, optimizing performance, and ensuring seamless integration with back-end services. My projects, such as EventEaze and Cultural Repository, demonstrate my proficiency in Flutter, Dart, and Firebase, showcasing my ability to deliver scalable, innovative solutions to complex problems. \nBeyond academics and professional engagements, I actively solve challenging problems on Leetcode (Top 50,000 globally) and GeeksForGeeks, with over 1,200 problems solved collectively. My contributions to open-source projects through GirlScript Summer of Code 2024 reflect my collaborative spirit and commitment to the tech community. \nI have been fortunate to receive numerous accolades, including a 100% scholarship under the STARS SCHEME and recognition for academic excellence through prestigious awards like the INSPIRE Award. With certifications in Postman API, SQL, and Networking, I continuously strive to enhance my technical skill set. \nPassionate about technology, learning, and innovation, I am eager to tackle real-world challenges and contribute to impactful projects. Let’s connect to explore opportunities to build something incredible together! 🚀",
	"chichenItzaHistoryInfo2": "The city was thought to have the most diverse population in the Maya world, a factor that could have contributed to this architectural variety.",
	"chichenItzaConstructionInfo1": "The structures of Chichen Itza were built from precisely chiseled limestone blocks that fit together perfectly without the mortar. Many of these stone buildings were originally painted in red, green, blue and purple colors depending on the availability of the pigments.\nThe stepped pyramid El Castillo stands about 98 feet (30 m) high and consists of a series of nine square terraces, each approximately 8.4 feet (2.57 m) high, with a 20 foot (6 m) high temple upon the summit.",
	"chichenItzaConstructionInfo2": "• Designed and maintained cross-platform application development using Flutter and Dart, prioritizing feature enhancements, user-friendly UI/UX, and seamless integration with RESTful APIs.\n• Implemented Git and GitLab for effective version control, facilitating smooth collaboration across development teams.\n• Successfully deployed mobile applications to Google Play Store, overseeing release cycles, resulting in a 5-10% performance improvement and a 10-15% reduction in app size.\n• Conducted API testing with Postman, ensuring seamless communication between front-end and back-end services.",
	"chichenItzaLocationInfo1": "Chichen Itza is located in the eastern portion of Yucatán state in Mexico. Nearby, four large sinkholes, called cenotes, could have provided plentiful water year round at Chichen, making it attractive for settlement.",
	"chichenItzaLocationInfo2": "Of these cenotes, the \"Cenote Sagrado\" or Sacred Cenote, was used for the sacrifice of precious objects and human beings as a form of worship to the Maya rain god Chaac.",
	"chichenItza600ce": "🎓 Integrated M.Tech in Cyber Security \n🏫 Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal \n📊 CGPA: 8.68/10 \n(Year of completion: e.g., 2026)",
	"chichenItza832ce": "🎓 Class 12th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📈 Percentage: 96% \n(Year completed: 2021)",
	"chichenItza998ce": "🎓 Class 10th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📉 Percentage: 95.8% \n(Year completed: 2019)",
	"chichenItza1100ce": "Chichen Itza declines as a regional center",
	"chichenItza1527ce": "Invaded by Spanish Conquistador Francisco de Montejo",
	"chichenItza1535ce": "All Spanish are driven from the Yucatán Peninsula",
