	"colosseumTitle": "Hey there! I’m Lalit Sahu, and I’m glad you’re here.",
	"colosseumSubTitle": "Welcome",
	"colosseumRegionTitle": "I'm from Indore",
	"colosseumArtifactCulture": "Roman",
	"colosseumArtifactGeolocation": "Roman Empire",
	"colosseumPullQuote1Top": "Still the Largest Standing",
	"colosseumPullQuote1Bottom": "Amphitheater in the World Today",
	"colosseumPullQuote2": "When falls the Coliseum, Rome shall fall; And when Rome falls - the World.",
	"colosseumPullQuote2Author": "Lord Byron",
	"colosseumCallout1": "It was used for gladiatorial contests and public spectacles including animal hunts, executions, reenactments of famous battles, and dramas based on Roman mythology, and mock sea battles.",
	"colosseumCallout2": "The Notary App, Application Developer, Bengaluru, India (Jul. 2024 - Oct. 2024)",
	"colosseumVideoCaption": "“Ancient Rome 101 | National Geographic.” Youtube, uploaded by National Geographic.",
	"colosseumMapCaption": "Map showing location of Colosseum in Rome, Italy,",
	"colosseumHistoryInfo1": "Hello! I’m Lalit Sahu, a passionate and driven software developer specializing in cross-platform application development and cybersecurity. Currently pursuing an Integrated MTech at Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal, I maintain a strong academic record with a CGPA of 8.68, and I am deeply committed to expanding my expertise in cutting-edge technologies. \nWith hands-on experience as an Application Developer at TheNotaryApp, I excel in creating user-centric applications, optimizing performance, and ensuring seamless integration with back-end services. My projects, such as EventEaze and Cultural Repository, demonstrate my proficiency in Flutter, Dart, and Firebase, showcasing my ability to deliver scalable, innovative solutions to complex problems. \nBeyond academics and professional engagements, I actively solve challenging problems on Leetcode (Top 50,000 globally) and GeeksForGeeks, with over 1,200 problems solved collectively. My contributions to open-source projects through GirlScript Summer of Code 2024 reflect my collaborative spirit and commitment to the tech community. \nI have been fortunate to receive numerous accolades, including a 100% scholarship under the STARS SCHEME and recognition for academic excellence through prestigious awards like the INSPIRE Award. With certifications in Postman API, SQL, and Networking, I continuously strive to enhance my technical skill set. \nPassionate about technology, learning, and innovation, I am eager to tackle real-world challenges and contribute to impactful projects. Let’s connect to explore opportunities to build something incredible together! 🚀",
	"colosseumHistoryInfo2": "The building ceased to be used for entertainment in the early medieval era. By the late 6th century a small chapel had been built into the structure of the amphitheater, and the arena was converted into a cemetery. \nThe numerous vaulted spaces in the arcades under the seating were converted into housing and workshops, and are recorded as still being rented out as late as the 12th century.",
	"colosseumConstructionInfo1": "Construction began under the emperor Vespasian (r. 69-79 CE) in 72 and was completed in 80 CE under his successor and heir, Titus (r. 79-81). Further modifications were made during the reign of Domitian (r. 81-96).\nThe Colosseum is built of travertine limestone, tuff (volcanic rock), and brick-faced concrete. The outer wall is estimated to have required over 3.5 million cubic feet of travertine stone which were set without mortar; they were held together by 300 tons of iron clamps.",
	"colosseumConstructionInfo2": "• Designed and maintained cross-platform application development using Flutter and Dart, prioritizing feature enhancements, user-friendly UI/UX, and seamless integration with RESTful APIs.\n• Implemented Git and GitLab for effective version control, facilitating smooth collaboration across development teams.\n• Successfully deployed mobile applications to Google Play Store, overseeing release cycles, resulting in a 5-10% performance improvement and a 10-15% reduction in app size.\n• Conducted API testing with Postman, ensuring seamless communication between front-end and back-end services.",
	"colosseumLocationInfo1": "Following the Great Fire of Rome in 64 CE, Emperor Nero seized much of the destroyed area to build his grandiose Domus Aurea (\"Golden House\"). A severe embarrassment to Nero's successors, parts of this extravagant palace and grounds, encompassing 1 sq mile, were filled with earth and built over.",
	"colosseumLocationInfo2": "On the site of the lake, in the middle of the palace grounds, Emperor Vespasian would build the Colosseum as part of a Roman resurgence.",
	"colosseum70ce": "🎓 Integrated M.Tech in Cyber Security \n🏫 Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal \n📊 CGPA: 8.68/10 \n(Year of completion: e.g., 2026)",
	"colosseum82ce": "🎓 Class 12th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📈 Percentage: 96% \n(Year completed: 2021)",
	"colosseum1140ce": "🎓 Class 10th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📉 Percentage: 95.8% \n(Year completed: 2019)",
	"colosseum1490ce": "Pope Alexander VI permitted the site to be used as a quarry, for both storing and salvaging building materials.",
	"colosseum1829ce": "Preservation of the colosseum officially began, after more than a millennia of dilapidation and vandalism. Pope Pius VIII was notably devoted to this project.",
	"colosseum1990ce": "A restoration project was undertaken to ensure the colosseum remained a major tourist attraction for Rome. It currently stands as one of the greatest sources of tourism revenue in Italy.",
	"colosseumCollectible1Title": "Glass hexagonal amphoriskos",
