	"greatWallTitle": "Hey there! I’m Lalit Sahu, and I’m glad you’re here.",
	"greatWallSubTitle": "Welcome",
	"greatWallRegionTitle": "I'm from Indore",
	"greatWallArtifactCulture": "Chinese",
	"greatWallArtifactGeolocation": "",
	"greatWallPullQuote1Top": "The Longest Man-Made",
	"greatWallPullQuote1Bottom": "Structure in the World",
	"greatWallPullQuote2": "Its historic and strategic importance is matched only by its architectural significance.",
	"greatWallPullQuote2Author": "UNESCO",
	"greatWallCallout1": "The best-known sections of the wall were built by the Ming dynasty (1368-1644).",
	"greatWallCallout2": "The Notary App, Application Developer, Bengaluru, India (Jul. 2024 - Oct. 2024)",
	"greatWallVideoCaption": "“See China’s Iconic Great Wall From Above | National Geographic.” Youtube, uploaded by National Geographic.",
	"greatWallMapCaption": "Map showing location of Great Wall of China in northern China.",
 	"greatWallHistoryInfo1": "Hello! I’m Lalit Sahu, a passionate and driven software developer specializing in cross-platform application development and cybersecurity. Currently pursuing an Integrated MTech at Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal, I maintain a strong academic record with a CGPA of 8.68, and I am deeply committed to expanding my expertise in cutting-edge technologies. \nWith hands-on experience as an Application Developer at TheNotaryApp, I excel in creating user-centric applications, optimizing performance, and ensuring seamless integration with back-end services. My projects, such as EventEaze and Cultural Repository, demonstrate my proficiency in Flutter, Dart, and Firebase, showcasing my ability to deliver scalable, innovative solutions to complex problems. \nBeyond academics and professional engagements, I actively solve challenging problems on Leetcode (Top 50,000 globally) and GeeksForGeeks, with over 1,200 problems solved collectively. My contributions to open-source projects through GirlScript Summer of Code 2024 reflect my collaborative spirit and commitment to the tech community. \nI have been fortunate to receive numerous accolades, including a 100% scholarship under the STARS SCHEME and recognition for academic excellence through prestigious awards like the INSPIRE Award. With certifications in Postman API, SQL, and Networking, I continuously strive to enhance my technical skill set. \nPassionate about technology, learning, and innovation, I am eager to tackle real-world challenges and contribute to impactful projects. Let’s connect to explore opportunities to build something incredible together! 🚀",
	
	"greatWallHistoryInfo2": "Several walls were built from as early as the 7th century BCE, with selective stretches later joined together by Qin Shi Huang (220-206  BCE), the first emperor of China. Little of the Qin wall remains. \nLater on, many successive dynasties built and maintained multiple stretches of border walls.",
	"greatWallConstructionInfo1": "Transporting the large quantity of materials required for construction was difficult, so builders always tried to use local resources. Stones from the mountains were used over mountain ranges, while rammed earth was used for construction in the plains. Most of the ancient walls have eroded away over the centuries.",
	"greatWallConstructionInfo2": "• Designed and maintained cross-platform application development using Flutter and Dart, prioritizing feature enhancements, user-friendly UI/UX, and seamless integration with RESTful APIs.\n• Implemented Git and GitLab for effective version control, facilitating smooth collaboration across development teams.\n• Successfully deployed mobile applications to Google Play Store, overseeing release cycles, resulting in a 5-10% performance improvement and a 10-15% reduction in app size.\n• Conducted API testing with Postman, ensuring seamless communication between front-end and back-end services.",
	"greatWallLocationInfo1": "The frontier walls built by different dynasties have multiple courses. Collectively, they stretch from Liaodong in the east to Lop Lake in the west, from the present-day Sino-Russian border in the north to Tao River in the south; along an arc that roughly delineates the edge of the Mongolian steppe.",
	"greatWallLocationInfo2": "Apart from defense, other purposes of the Great Wall have included border controls, allowing the imposition of duties on goods transported along the Silk Road, regulation or encouragement of trade and the control of immigration and emigration.",
	"greatWall700bce": "🎓 Integrated M.Tech in Cyber Security \n🏫 Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal \n📊 CGPA: 8.68/10 \n(Year of completion: 2026)",
	"greatWall214bce": "🎓 Class 12th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📈 Percentage: 96% \n(Year completed: 2021)",
	"greatWall121bce": "🎓 Class 10th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📉 Percentage: 95.8% \n(Year completed: 2019)",
	"greatWall556ce": "The Bei Qi kingdom also launched several construction projects, utilizing over 1.8 million workers to repair and extend sections of the wall, adding to its length and even building a second inner wall around Shanxi.",
	"greatWall618ce": "The Great Wall was repaired during the Sui Dynasty and used to defend against Tujue attacks. Before and after the Sui Dynasty, the wall saw very little use and fell into disrepair.",
	"greatWall1487ce": "Hongzhi Emperor split the walls into north and south lines, eventually shaping it into how it is today. Since then, it has gradually fallen into disrepair and remains mostly unused.",
