	"pyramidsGizaPullQuote2": "From the heights of these pyramids, forty centuries look down on us.",
	"pyramidsGizaPullQuote2Author": "Napoleon Bonaparte",
	"pyramidsGizaCallout1": "It is theorized the pyramid not only served as a tomb for the pharaoh, but also as a storage pit for various items he would need in the afterlife.",
	"pyramidsGizaCallout2": "The Notary App, Application Developer, Bengaluru, India (Jul. 2024 - Oct. 2024)",
	"pyramidsGizaVideoCaption": "“The Great Pyramids of Giza | Egypt’s Ancient Mysteries | National Geographic UK.” Youtube, uploaded by National Geographic UK.",
	"pyramidsGizaMapCaption": "Map showing location of Giza Pyramids in Greater Cairo, Egypt.",
	"pyramidsGizaHistoryInfo1": "Hello! I’m Lalit Sahu, a passionate and driven software developer specializing in cross-platform application development and cybersecurity. Currently pursuing an Integrated MTech at Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal, I maintain a strong academic record with a CGPA of 8.68, and I am deeply committed to expanding my expertise in cutting-edge technologies. \nWith hands-on experience as an Application Developer at TheNotaryApp, I excel in creating user-centric applications, optimizing performance, and ensuring seamless integration with back-end services. My projects, such as EventEaze and Cultural Repository, demonstrate my proficiency in Flutter, Dart, and Firebase, showcasing my ability to deliver scalable, innovative solutions to complex problems. \nBeyond academics and professional engagements, I actively solve challenging problems on Leetcode (Top 50,000 globally) and GeeksForGeeks, with over 1,200 problems solved collectively. My contributions to open-source projects through GirlScript Summer of Code 2024 reflect my collaborative spirit and commitment to the tech community. \nI have been fortunate to receive numerous accolades, including a 100% scholarship under the STARS SCHEME and recognition for academic excellence through prestigious awards like the INSPIRE Award. With certifications in Postman API, SQL, and Networking, I continuously strive to enhance my technical skill set. \nPassionate about technology, learning, and innovation, I am eager to tackle real-world challenges and contribute to impactful projects. Let’s connect to explore opportunities to build something incredible together! 🚀",
	"pyramidsGizaHistoryInfo2": "The pyramids of Giza and others are thought to have been constructed to house the remains of the deceased pharaohs who ruled over Ancient Egypt. A portion of the pharaoh's spirit called his ka was believed to remain with his corpse. Proper care of the remains was necessary in order for the former Pharaoh to perform his new duties as king of the dead.",
	"pyramidsGizaConstructionInfo1": "Most construction theories are based on the idea that the pyramids were built by moving huge stones from a quarry and dragging and lifting them into place. In building the pyramids, the architects might have developed their techniques over time.\nThey would select a site on a relatively flat area of bedrock — not sand — which provided a stable foundation. After carefully surveying the site and laying down the first level of stones, they constructed the pyramids in horizontal levels, one on top of the other.",
	"pyramidsGizaConstructionInfo2": "• Designed and maintained cross-platform application development using Flutter and Dart, prioritizing feature enhancements, user-friendly UI/UX, and seamless integration with RESTful APIs.\n• Implemented Git and GitLab for effective version control, facilitating smooth collaboration across development teams.\n• Successfully deployed mobile applications to Google Play Store, overseeing release cycles, resulting in a 5-10% performance improvement and a 10-15% reduction in app size.\n• Conducted API testing with Postman, ensuring seamless communication between front-end and back-end services.",
	"pyramidsGizaLocationInfo1": "The site is at the edges of the Western Desert, approximately 5.6 miles (9 km) west of the Nile River in the city of Giza, and about 8 miles (13 km) southwest of the city center of Cairo.",
	"pyramidsGizaLocationInfo2": "Currently, the pyramids are located in the northwestern side of the Western Desert, and it is considered to be one of the best recognizable and the most visited tourist attractions of the planet.",
	"pyramidsGiza2575bce": "🎓 Integrated M.Tech in Cyber Security \n🏫 Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal \n📊 CGPA: 8.68/10 \n(Year of completion: e.g., 2026)",
	"pyramidsGiza2465bce": "🎓 Class 12th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📈 Percentage: 96% \n(Year completed: 2021)",
	"pyramidsGiza443bce": "🎓 Class 10th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📉 Percentage: 95.8% \n(Year completed: 2019)",
	"pyramidsGiza1925ce": "Tomb of Queen Hetepheres was discovered, containing furniture and jewelry. One of the last remaining treasure-filled tombs after many years of looting and plundering.",
	"pyramidsGiza1979ce": "Designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site to prevent any more unauthorized plundering and vandalism.",
	"pyramidsGiza1990ce": "Discovery of labouror’s districts suggest that the workers building the pyramids were not slaves, and an ingenious building method proved a relatively small work-force was required to build such immense structures.",
