	"tajMahalVideoCaption": "“India’s Taj Mahal Is an Enduring Monument to Love | National Geographic.” Youtube, uploaded by National Geographic.",
	"tajMahalMapCaption": "Map showing location of Taj Mahal in Uttar Pradesh, India.",
	"tajMahalHistoryInfo1": "Hello! I’m Lalit Sahu, a passionate and driven software developer specializing in cross-platform application development and cybersecurity. Currently pursuing an Integrated MTech at Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal, I maintain a strong academic record with a CGPA of 8.68, and I am deeply committed to expanding my expertise in cutting-edge technologies. \nWith hands-on experience as an Application Developer at TheNotaryApp, I excel in creating user-centric applications, optimizing performance, and ensuring seamless integration with back-end services. My projects, such as EventEaze and Cultural Repository, demonstrate my proficiency in Flutter, Dart, and Firebase, showcasing my ability to deliver scalable, innovative solutions to complex problems. \nBeyond academics and professional engagements, I actively solve challenging problems on Leetcode (Top 50,000 globally) and GeeksForGeeks, with over 1,200 problems solved collectively. My contributions to open-source projects through GirlScript Summer of Code 2024 reflect my collaborative spirit and commitment to the tech community. \nI have been fortunate to receive numerous accolades, including a 100% scholarship under the STARS SCHEME and recognition for academic excellence through prestigious awards like the INSPIRE Award. With certifications in Postman API, SQL, and Networking, I continuously strive to enhance my technical skill set. \nPassionate about technology, learning, and innovation, I am eager to tackle real-world challenges and contribute to impactful projects. Let’s connect to explore opportunities to build something incredible together! 🚀",
	"tajMahalHistoryInfo2": "The tomb is the centerpiece of a 42-acre (17-hectare) complex, which include twin mosque buildings (placed symmetrically on either side of the mausoleum), a guest house, and is set in formal gardens bounded on three sides by walls.",
	"tajMahalConstructionInfo1": "The Taj Mahal was constructed using materials from all over India and Asia. It is believed over 1,000 elephants were used to transport building materials.\nThe translucent white marble was brought from Rajasthan, the jasper from Punjab, jade and crystal from China. The turquoise was from Tibet and the lapis from Afghanistan, while the sapphire came from Sri Lanka. In all, twenty-eight types of precious and semi-precious stones were inlaid into the white marble.",
	"tajMahalConstructionInfo2": "• Designed and maintained cross-platform application development using Flutter and Dart, prioritizing feature enhancements, user-friendly UI/UX, and seamless integration with RESTful APIs.\n• Implemented Git and GitLab for effective version control, facilitating smooth collaboration across development teams.\n• Successfully deployed mobile applications to Google Play Store, overseeing release cycles, resulting in a 5-10% performance improvement and a 10-15% reduction in app size.\n• Conducted API testing with Postman, ensuring seamless communication between front-end and back-end services.",
	"tajMahalLocationInfo1": "India's most famed building, it is situated in the eastern part of the city on the southern bank of the Yamuna River, nearly 1 mile east of the Agra Fort, also on the right bank of the Yamuna.",
	"tajMahalLocationInfo2": "The Taj Mahal is built on a parcel of land to the south of the walled city of Agra. Shah Jahan presented Maharaja Jai Singh with a large palace in the center of Agra in exchange for the land.",
	"tajMahal1631ce": "🎓 Integrated M.Tech in Cyber Security \n🏫 Vellore Institute of Technology, Bhopal \n📊 CGPA: 8.68/10 \n(Year of completion: e.g., 2026)",
	"tajMahal1647ce": "🎓 Class 12th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📈 Percentage: 96% \n(Year completed: 2021)",
	"tajMahal1658ce": "🎓 Class 10th \n🏫 Government Excellence H.S. School, Guna \n📉 Percentage: 95.8% \n(Year completed: 2019)",
	"tajMahal1901ce": "Lord Curzon and the British Viceroy of India carried out a major restoration to the monument after over 350 years of decay and corrosion due to factory pollution and exhaust.",
	"tajMahal1984ce": "To protect the structure from Sikh militants and some Hindu nationalist groups, night viewing was banned to tourists. This ban would last 20 years.",
	"tajMahal1998ce": "Restoration and research program put into action to help preserve the monument.",
